1
00:00:04,105 --> 00:00:05,865
You're roommates, so I don't mind.

2
00:00:05,945 --> 00:00:07,705
But you're not dating, right?

3
00:00:07,785 --> 00:00:09,825
This week's club mission is to help him.

4
00:00:09,905 --> 00:00:11,065
You need something new.

5
00:00:11,145 --> 00:00:12,265
Once you try something new,

6
00:00:12,345 --> 00:00:13,585
it'll be easier to forget the past.

7
00:00:13,665 --> 00:00:14,665
Don't lose to the voice in your head.

8
00:00:14,745 --> 00:00:15,825
I made that rule myself.

9
00:00:15,905 --> 00:00:17,785
And he already likes someone.

10
00:00:17,865 --> 00:00:18,905
Don't you feel anything at all?

11
00:00:20,905 --> 00:00:24,265
What inspired you to confess to Summer?

12
00:00:24,345 --> 00:00:27,305
<i>It may sound cliché,</i>
<i>but I'd regret it if I never told her.</i>

13
00:00:27,385 --> 00:00:30,785
<i>I like you.</i>
<i>Break the rule and be my boyfriend.</i>

14
00:00:30,865 --> 00:00:32,145
<i>Will you open your heart to me?</i>

15
00:00:33,465 --> 00:00:34,385
As my boyfriend.

16
00:00:38,865 --> 00:00:40,785
<i>Go for it. Charge in!</i>

17
00:00:40,865 --> 00:00:43,345
-<i>Go!</i>
-<i>Hey! Down there!</i>

18
00:00:43,425 --> 00:00:44,825
<i>Hey! Ter! Ter!</i>

19
00:00:44,905 --> 00:00:45,825
<i>He's going down!</i>

20
00:00:45,905 --> 00:00:46,825
Yeah, that's it! Nice!

21
00:00:46,905 --> 00:00:48,425
Nice! We've got the advantage!

22
00:00:48,505 --> 00:00:50,705
-Hit him! Hit him!
-Ter! Down there!

23
00:00:50,785 --> 00:00:53,705
-<i>He's in! He's in!</i>
-He's going for the kill!

24
00:00:53,785 --> 00:00:55,785
<i>That's it! That's it!</i>

25
00:00:55,865 --> 00:00:58,025
Ter is on fire.

26
00:00:58,105 --> 00:01:00,425
I totally ship them. They're even
using the same Discord account.

27
00:01:00,505 --> 00:01:02,145
Even Leo and Neo use separate accounts.

28
00:01:02,225 --> 00:01:04,225
Come on, damn it. Let us have some space.

29
00:01:04,305 --> 00:01:05,665
We're practically glued together 24/7.

30
00:01:08,065 --> 00:01:09,345
Yeah,

31
00:01:09,425 --> 00:01:11,425
-this is my last game.
-Mine too.

32
00:01:12,065 --> 00:01:13,145
This is my last match too.

33
00:01:16,705 --> 00:01:17,545
What's with you?

34
00:01:18,145 --> 00:01:19,425
If you're sleepy, just sleep here.

35
00:01:20,145 --> 00:01:21,545
We've been dating for less than a month,

36
00:01:21,625 --> 00:01:22,545
and you're already asking me
to sleep with you.

37
00:01:23,145 --> 00:01:24,265
You idiot.

38
00:01:24,345 --> 00:01:26,625
What are you thinking?
I just meant sleeping.

39
00:01:27,585 --> 00:01:29,785
Wait until we've been together for a year,
then I'll sleep with you.

40
00:01:30,705 --> 00:01:32,225
You're so damn adorable.

41
00:01:33,385 --> 00:01:34,585
LeeIth, that's enough.

42
00:01:37,225 --> 00:01:38,225
Where are you going?

43
00:01:39,585 --> 00:01:41,625
Just act natural
when we go to school tomorrow.

44
00:01:42,225 --> 00:01:43,825
Then let me get my fill of you first.

45
00:01:44,545 --> 00:01:45,385
Get your fill of what?

46
00:01:48,585 --> 00:01:49,665
That's enough.

47
00:01:50,585 --> 00:01:51,785
Hey, that's enough.

48
00:01:51,865 --> 00:01:52,985
You're acting like a dog.

49
00:01:53,065 --> 00:01:54,625
Stop. You're acting like a dog.

50
00:01:54,705 --> 00:01:56,465
-That's enough.
-That's because I'm your puppy.

51
00:01:56,545 --> 00:01:58,745
LeeIth! Ter! Hello? Are you guys there?

52
00:01:59,425 --> 00:02:00,585
<i>Come on, put in some effort.</i>

53
00:02:00,665 --> 00:02:01,625
<i>Hello?</i>

54
00:02:01,705 --> 00:02:03,225
<i>Hey, don't go quiet, asshole.</i>

55
00:02:03,305 --> 00:02:05,145
<i>You two aren't doing something, are you?</i>

56
00:02:06,025 --> 00:02:07,505
I just went to take a leak, and…

57
00:02:07,585 --> 00:02:08,785
Ter's going to bed.

58
00:02:08,864 --> 00:02:10,744
Nothing's going on. Nothing…

59
00:02:12,425 --> 00:02:13,425
I'm off to bed, guys.

60
00:02:13,505 --> 00:02:14,585
-Okay, bye.
-Okay.

61
00:02:14,665 --> 00:02:15,865
-See you.
-Okay.

62
00:02:17,265 --> 00:02:18,345
I'm going to bed.

63
00:02:19,905 --> 00:02:21,065
Sweet dreams.

64
00:02:23,025 --> 00:02:24,425
Remember to act natural tomorrow.

65
00:02:24,505 --> 00:02:27,265
-Got it?
-Okay, you should go now.

66
00:02:27,345 --> 00:02:28,625
-Bye.
-Sweet dreams.

67
00:02:28,705 --> 00:02:29,705
Sweet dreams.

68
00:02:32,705 --> 00:02:34,345
That hit way too hard.

69
00:02:34,425 --> 00:02:36,065
How am I supposed to survive this?

70
00:02:40,865 --> 00:02:43,425
You're taking the fitness test.
Stay focused.

71
00:02:43,505 --> 00:02:44,505
Yes, Sir.

72
00:02:50,945 --> 00:02:52,225
Okay.

73
00:03:04,265 --> 00:03:06,385
Stop. Someone will see us.

74
00:03:07,145 --> 00:03:08,385
Putter.

75
00:03:09,545 --> 00:03:11,545
Where are you rushing off to?

76
00:03:13,585 --> 00:03:14,585
Huh?

77
00:03:15,785 --> 00:03:17,305
You're acting weird.

78
00:03:17,385 --> 00:03:19,425
Did something happen during the break?

79
00:03:19,505 --> 00:03:21,265
Why do you look so cheerful?

80
00:03:21,345 --> 00:03:23,665
Yeah. Are you in love or something?

81
00:03:25,345 --> 00:03:28,225
What? I just saw something funny.

82
00:03:29,705 --> 00:03:31,585
-What was so funny?
-Yeah, what was so funny?

83
00:03:43,945 --> 00:03:45,305
Hey, I need to pee.

84
00:03:46,185 --> 00:03:47,545
Then pee.

85
00:03:47,625 --> 00:03:48,865
I've already seen it all.

86
00:03:53,745 --> 00:03:54,905
What the hell are you doing?

87
00:03:54,985 --> 00:03:56,745
I'm here to take a shower.

88
00:03:57,345 --> 00:03:58,985
What are you embarrassed about?
I've got one too.

89
00:03:59,065 --> 00:04:00,625
Hey, idiot! Get out!

90
00:04:08,385 --> 00:04:10,145
Don't forget to fix the door lock.

91
00:04:14,585 --> 00:04:15,585
It doesn't need fixing.

92
00:04:16,825 --> 00:04:19,184
No need to lock it. We're dating now.

93
00:04:20,665 --> 00:04:23,385
Even if we're dating,
shouldn't we still have some boundaries?

94
00:04:24,265 --> 00:04:26,265
Okay, my boyfriend.

95
00:04:26,945 --> 00:04:29,185
Move aside. I need to dry my hands.

96
00:04:54,105 --> 00:04:55,905
Go pee too, LeeIth.

97
00:04:55,985 --> 00:04:56,985
Yeah, coming.

98
00:05:18,225 --> 00:05:19,185
Move.

99
00:05:21,105 --> 00:05:23,225
-Move over.
-Yeah, scoot over.

100
00:05:23,305 --> 00:05:25,705
Damn, you two took forever in there.

101
00:05:25,785 --> 00:05:27,425
What the hell were you guys doing?

102
00:05:36,665 --> 00:05:38,185
What?

103
00:05:38,265 --> 00:05:39,585
Is spending a long time
in the bathroom a crime?

104
00:05:45,625 --> 00:05:47,465
-What the hell are you looking at?
-You wanna go?

105
00:05:47,545 --> 00:05:49,065
-Asshole.
-You looking for a fight?

106
00:05:49,145 --> 00:05:51,585
-You wanna fight?
-You wanna go?

107
00:05:55,025 --> 00:05:56,345
Get him!

108
00:07:26,705 --> 00:07:27,705
I'm starving.

109
00:07:27,785 --> 00:07:28,825
Where's your twin?

110
00:07:28,905 --> 00:07:29,985
Where'd the other one go?

111
00:07:30,745 --> 00:07:31,785
He's shy around girls.

112
00:07:31,865 --> 00:07:35,065
He's over there eating by himself.

113
00:07:38,625 --> 00:07:40,105
I have a plan.

114
00:07:40,185 --> 00:07:42,385
-Huh? What?
-I know what to do.

115
00:07:42,465 --> 00:07:45,105
Hey, Leo. My friends have forgiven you.

116
00:07:45,185 --> 00:07:46,465
You're welcome to join us at our table.

117
00:07:46,545 --> 00:07:48,545
Or should we come eat with you?

118
00:07:48,625 --> 00:07:50,585
How about it? Go on, go.

119
00:07:50,665 --> 00:07:52,065
Go on. Go.

120
00:07:52,145 --> 00:07:54,785
I'll go myself. Hang on.

121
00:07:54,865 --> 00:07:56,865
-He's coming.
-It actually worked.

122
00:07:58,585 --> 00:07:59,945
-Hey.
-Sit here, dumbass.

123
00:08:00,025 --> 00:08:01,345
-We're all friends.
-Have a seat.

124
00:08:01,425 --> 00:08:03,025
Hi.

125
00:08:03,825 --> 00:08:05,745
I'll sit somewhere else.

126
00:08:07,225 --> 00:08:08,705
-He's really shy.
-Told you.

127
00:08:08,785 --> 00:08:12,425
-He's ridiculously shy.
-Your delivery is here.

128
00:08:12,505 --> 00:08:14,505
You're so sweet. Thank you.

129
00:08:16,305 --> 00:08:17,745
Guys, come here.

130
00:08:18,945 --> 00:08:21,345
When did those two make up?

131
00:08:22,305 --> 00:08:23,705
After the concert at Siam,

132
00:08:23,785 --> 00:08:25,945
they made a huge public apology
to each other online.

133
00:08:27,065 --> 00:08:28,865
Classic.

134
00:08:28,945 --> 00:08:30,145
Same old ending.

135
00:08:30,985 --> 00:08:32,505
Hey,

136
00:08:32,585 --> 00:08:34,545
you're gossiping right in front of us.

137
00:08:34,625 --> 00:08:36,664
We weren't gossiping, were we?

138
00:08:36,745 --> 00:08:39,545
Nobody was gossiping.
We were just keeping everyone informed.

139
00:08:39,625 --> 00:08:41,505
Just making sure everyone knows.

140
00:08:43,664 --> 00:08:44,865
Oh, right, Proud.

141
00:08:44,945 --> 00:08:45,945
I never got to tell you.

142
00:08:46,025 --> 00:08:47,025
You were so cool that day.

143
00:08:47,105 --> 00:08:48,265
Thanks, Indy.

144
00:08:48,345 --> 00:08:50,145
-Let's hang out together sometime.
-Sure.

145
00:08:51,145 --> 00:08:52,145
What? You want to steal her from me?

146
00:08:52,825 --> 00:08:53,865
Hey, hey!

147
00:08:53,945 --> 00:08:55,905
BeReal, everyone! BeReal!

148
00:08:57,145 --> 00:08:59,345
-Here we go.
-Okay, one, two, three.

149
00:09:01,065 --> 00:09:02,065
Okay.

150
00:09:02,905 --> 00:09:04,785
-What is that?
-So cute.

151
00:09:06,185 --> 00:09:07,225
What is it?

152
00:09:08,385 --> 00:09:11,385
It's kind of like Instagram.
You explain it.

153
00:09:11,465 --> 00:09:13,345
It randomly gives you a two-minute timer

154
00:09:13,425 --> 00:09:15,265
to take a real, unfiltered photo.

155
00:09:15,345 --> 00:09:17,145
It uses both the front
and rear cameras at the same time

156
00:09:17,225 --> 00:09:18,425
to capture the moment as a memory.

157
00:09:19,305 --> 00:09:21,025
You're so smart, babe.

158
00:09:21,105 --> 00:09:22,185
Do guys use it too?

159
00:09:22,265 --> 00:09:24,145
It was huge for a while.

160
00:09:24,225 --> 00:09:26,505
It's not as popular now,

161
00:09:26,585 --> 00:09:28,265
but it's still pretty good.

162
00:09:28,345 --> 00:09:30,185
-Bring your food over here.
-It captures little moments.

163
00:09:30,265 --> 00:09:31,745
You don't have to order
the same thing as me next time.

164
00:09:31,825 --> 00:09:33,265
I didn't copy you. I always order this.

165
00:09:33,345 --> 00:09:35,105
Then why'd you bring
your food over if you didn't?

166
00:09:36,425 --> 00:09:37,705
Are you seriously just eating rice?

167
00:09:37,785 --> 00:09:39,865
-Yeah, this is enough for me.
-Come on, don't argue.

168
00:09:41,225 --> 00:09:42,425
What did you bring?

169
00:09:47,865 --> 00:09:49,825
-What's that?
-Looks delicious.

170
00:09:49,905 --> 00:09:51,065
Is that healthy food?

171
00:09:51,145 --> 00:09:52,225
-Did you make it yourself?
-It looks so good.

172
00:09:54,785 --> 00:09:56,905
-You're amazing.
-That's good.

173
00:09:56,985 --> 00:09:59,185
This is way better
than your blended chicken breast.

174
00:09:59,265 --> 00:10:00,905
It makes me want to throw up
every time I see it.

175
00:10:00,985 --> 00:10:02,105
Why would you say that?

176
00:10:02,185 --> 00:10:04,185
Seriously, it's really good.

177
00:10:04,265 --> 00:10:06,425
Go ahead. Here's the chicken breast dish.

178
00:10:07,465 --> 00:10:09,265
What do you think, Chef? Give it a try.

179
00:10:13,025 --> 00:10:14,225
How is it?

180
00:10:15,705 --> 00:10:16,545
Nine out of ten.

181
00:10:16,625 --> 00:10:17,985
Hey, what about the last point?

182
00:10:18,065 --> 00:10:19,865
If I give you a perfect score,
you'll get cocky.

183
00:10:20,905 --> 00:10:22,105
Okay, fair enough.

184
00:10:23,745 --> 00:10:25,305
Isn't it a bit bland?

185
00:10:26,745 --> 00:10:29,545
Come on, hurry up. Eat it.

186
00:10:29,625 --> 00:10:30,705
Let me have some too.

187
00:10:31,865 --> 00:10:32,985
-I'll take this piece.
-Can you make this for me sometime?

188
00:10:33,065 --> 00:10:35,545
Are the vegetables cooked?
LeeIth, give them a try.

189
00:10:35,625 --> 00:10:36,825
I'm good.

190
00:10:36,905 --> 00:10:38,345
I don't want to steal Ter's food.

191
00:10:38,905 --> 00:10:40,185
You can tell it's good
just by looking at it.

192
00:10:41,985 --> 00:10:43,185
Then I'll eat it myself.

193
00:10:43,265 --> 00:10:44,185
Yeah, me too.

194
00:10:45,985 --> 00:10:48,385
Actually, it's still a little undercooked.

195
00:10:48,945 --> 00:10:50,305
True.

196
00:10:50,385 --> 00:10:52,705
-You're right.
-The vegetables are really bland.

197
00:10:52,785 --> 00:10:54,585
Hey, don't be discouraged.

198
00:10:54,665 --> 00:10:56,105
I actually like it this way.

199
00:11:06,225 --> 00:11:08,265
Alright. Werewolves, open your eyes.

200
00:11:12,865 --> 00:11:15,025
I can tell.
Indy definitely opened his eyes.

201
00:11:16,665 --> 00:11:17,785
Then prove it.

202
00:11:19,545 --> 00:11:21,465
I don't believe you. Just wait and see.

203
00:11:21,545 --> 00:11:22,625
That's enough, you guys.

204
00:11:23,345 --> 00:11:24,785
Werewolves, close your eyes.

205
00:11:26,345 --> 00:11:29,345
Seer, open your eyes.

206
00:11:30,745 --> 00:11:32,265
Who would you like to check
on the first night?

207
00:11:39,385 --> 00:11:40,465
But…

208
00:11:46,905 --> 00:11:49,465
Seer, stop taking so long. Hurry up.

209
00:11:49,545 --> 00:11:50,505
I'm about to fall asleep, damn it.

210
00:11:52,265 --> 00:11:53,585
Seer, close your eyes.

211
00:11:53,665 --> 00:11:54,945
Done, done, done.

212
00:11:55,025 --> 00:11:56,665
Alright, everyone, open your eyes.

213
00:11:59,425 --> 00:12:01,105
The werewolves win.

214
00:12:05,265 --> 00:12:06,985
Damn, I can't trust anyone.

215
00:12:07,065 --> 00:12:08,945
-You're so sneaky.
-I lost all eight rounds.

216
00:12:10,625 --> 00:12:12,505
How am I supposed
to trust you guys after this?

217
00:12:12,585 --> 00:12:15,145
You guys are so good at lying.
I don't want to play anymore.

218
00:12:15,225 --> 00:12:16,785
-Me neither.
-I'm innocent.

219
00:12:16,865 --> 00:12:18,305
I was the moderator.

220
00:12:19,425 --> 00:12:21,185
You sneaky little bastard.

221
00:12:21,265 --> 00:12:23,105
-Never saw that coming.
-Time's up, isn't it?

222
00:12:24,545 --> 00:12:26,585
School's giving us tomorrow off
for exam prep.

223
00:12:26,665 --> 00:12:28,345
Where are you guys studying?

224
00:12:28,425 --> 00:12:29,665
Should we study together?

225
00:12:29,745 --> 00:12:31,425
LeeIth and I always form a study group.

226
00:12:31,505 --> 00:12:34,225
Damn, every time I come here,

227
00:12:34,305 --> 00:12:36,305
we never actually study.
We just mess around.

228
00:12:36,385 --> 00:12:38,705
It's called study-life balance.

229
00:12:40,305 --> 00:12:42,345
Hey, this time I want to study at home.

230
00:12:42,425 --> 00:12:45,145
My mom will kill me otherwise.
You're such a wimp.

231
00:12:45,225 --> 00:12:47,505
Let's wait and study together
for finals instead.

232
00:12:49,025 --> 00:12:51,265
-No, no, no.
-Calm down.

233
00:12:51,345 --> 00:12:53,105
We're outside. Take it easy.

234
00:12:53,185 --> 00:12:54,465
What about you, Ter?

235
00:12:59,425 --> 00:13:00,625
I'll just study at home.

236
00:13:01,705 --> 00:13:02,705
I get distracted easily.

237
00:13:04,305 --> 00:13:05,305
That's depressing.

238
00:13:06,705 --> 00:13:08,305
Come on, one more round.

239
00:13:08,385 --> 00:13:10,545
Now that you're over your heartbreak,
you're all fired up.

240
00:13:10,625 --> 00:13:12,105
Are you making fun of me?

241
00:13:12,185 --> 00:13:13,265
Easy, easy.

242
00:13:13,345 --> 00:13:14,785
-Calm down, Bro.
-Easy, easy.

243
00:13:15,825 --> 00:13:17,505
Hey, hey. I'm sorry.

244
00:13:17,585 --> 00:13:19,825
-I'm sorry.
-Don't fight.

245
00:13:19,905 --> 00:13:21,665
Come on!

246
00:13:25,665 --> 00:13:27,065
I'm bored.

247
00:13:41,905 --> 00:13:42,905
That's BeReal.

248
00:13:44,585 --> 00:13:46,345
Why didn't you tell everyone you use it?

249
00:13:46,985 --> 00:13:48,265
Because I wanted to keep it to myself.

250
00:13:50,665 --> 00:13:51,945
Hey.

251
00:13:52,025 --> 00:13:53,265
Take a picture of me.

252
00:13:53,345 --> 00:13:56,825
-Come on, take one of me. Hurry.
-Yeah, sure.

253
00:14:05,825 --> 00:14:07,745
Damn. Too real.

254
00:14:08,545 --> 00:14:09,545
Let me see.

255
00:14:13,905 --> 00:14:16,065
Yep, that's totally me.

256
00:14:22,065 --> 00:14:23,425
You've been using it for a long time.

257
00:14:25,025 --> 00:14:26,945
Yeah. Since before
I transferred to this school.

258
00:14:28,025 --> 00:14:29,065
Huh?

259
00:14:29,145 --> 00:14:30,505
Was this from the first day of school?

260
00:14:30,585 --> 00:14:31,785
This one.

261
00:14:32,385 --> 00:14:34,025
-Look, look.
-You remember?

262
00:14:38,105 --> 00:14:39,705
Well, meeting someone like you…

263
00:14:40,585 --> 00:14:41,785
isn't something I'd forget.

264
00:14:43,065 --> 00:14:45,305
-Was I cute?
-Yeah.

265
00:14:46,585 --> 00:14:48,865
You're not even going to play along?

266
00:14:50,785 --> 00:14:51,785
Then set it up again.

267
00:14:53,225 --> 00:14:55,385
So… Was I cute?

268
00:14:56,545 --> 00:14:57,505
Yeah.

269
00:15:00,545 --> 00:15:02,185
What's with you?

270
00:15:02,265 --> 00:15:03,465
You're so whipped.

271
00:15:03,545 --> 00:15:06,465
So, when are you actually going to study?

272
00:15:11,025 --> 00:15:11,865
That hurt.

273
00:15:12,425 --> 00:15:13,265
What was that for?

274
00:15:13,345 --> 00:15:14,825
When, then?

275
00:15:14,905 --> 00:15:16,545
How's anything going to stick
if you don't study?

276
00:15:16,625 --> 00:15:19,345
You ditched your friends,
and you're still not studying.

277
00:15:19,425 --> 00:15:21,425
Go check the CCTV footage.

278
00:15:21,505 --> 00:15:24,025
I said I'd study at home,

279
00:15:24,105 --> 00:15:25,825
but I never said I'd study seriously.

280
00:15:33,265 --> 00:15:34,945
Studying at home…

281
00:15:35,985 --> 00:15:37,865
really is more comfortable
than studying outside.

282
00:15:48,225 --> 00:15:49,665
What's with you?

283
00:15:52,025 --> 00:15:53,345
Is that a new perfume?

284
00:15:54,705 --> 00:15:56,265
Yeah. What do you think?

285
00:15:59,265 --> 00:16:00,545
Well, it's new.

286
00:16:00,625 --> 00:16:02,665
But your old one was more popular.

287
00:16:03,185 --> 00:16:04,625
Indy uses this one too.

288
00:16:08,145 --> 00:16:09,585
Can you even solve these problems?

289
00:16:10,465 --> 00:16:12,985
I have no idea. Can you teach me?

290
00:16:13,705 --> 00:16:16,265
-Yeah. Come down and I'll teach you.
-No.

291
00:16:18,745 --> 00:16:20,905
Come down here. Come on.

292
00:16:20,985 --> 00:16:22,865
Can you get down properly?

293
00:16:24,865 --> 00:16:26,105
Come on.

294
00:16:29,545 --> 00:16:30,465
Watch me.

295
00:16:30,545 --> 00:16:32,385
See this one? See this problem?

296
00:16:32,465 --> 00:16:34,425
You solve it the same way.

297
00:16:34,505 --> 00:16:35,465
You'll get this.

298
00:16:40,625 --> 00:16:44,185
I never thought
I'd end up living with a genius.

299
00:16:44,265 --> 00:16:46,865
At first, all you did was play games
and draw all day.

300
00:16:48,025 --> 00:16:49,785
I never thought you'd be this smart.

301
00:16:52,105 --> 00:16:54,305
You're so dramatic.

302
00:16:54,385 --> 00:16:56,065
Seriously, so dramatic.

303
00:16:56,145 --> 00:16:57,945
-So dramatic.
-Yeah.

304
00:16:58,745 --> 00:17:00,265
I am dramatic.

305
00:17:10,305 --> 00:17:11,944
These days,

306
00:17:12,545 --> 00:17:14,065
you've got quite a sweet tooth.

307
00:17:14,145 --> 00:17:15,825
Keep it up, and they'll have to
amputate your leg.

308
00:17:17,065 --> 00:17:19,265
Whenever I say something, I mean it.

309
00:17:19,345 --> 00:17:21,265
Someone like you

310
00:17:21,345 --> 00:17:22,665
could easily become a doctor.

311
00:17:22,745 --> 00:17:24,224
Whoa, a doctor?

312
00:17:24,785 --> 00:17:25,865
Damn.

313
00:17:26,585 --> 00:17:28,265
That never even crossed my mind.

314
00:17:30,225 --> 00:17:32,825
So, why did you choose architecture?

315
00:17:35,385 --> 00:17:37,945
Honestly,
I wanted to become an esports player.

316
00:17:38,625 --> 00:17:41,025
But my family is all about art,

317
00:17:41,105 --> 00:17:42,465
so I had to study architecture.

318
00:17:43,585 --> 00:17:44,665
That makes sense.

319
00:17:45,345 --> 00:17:47,185
I have to study engineering
because of my dad too.

320
00:17:50,065 --> 00:17:52,105
That's why I wanted to study in Bangkok.

321
00:17:52,185 --> 00:17:53,865
I wanted to get away from them.

322
00:17:54,385 --> 00:17:56,105
When you're chasing your dream,

323
00:17:56,185 --> 00:17:58,065
having to hide it all the time…

324
00:17:58,145 --> 00:17:59,385
is suffocating.

325
00:18:00,745 --> 00:18:01,945
From now on,

326
00:18:02,465 --> 00:18:04,545
I'll be your number one supporter

327
00:18:04,625 --> 00:18:06,385
and your very first fan.

328
00:18:07,185 --> 00:18:09,305
I'll be cheering you on
at every match from the front row.

329
00:18:10,985 --> 00:18:12,825
You're so dramatic.

330
00:18:12,905 --> 00:18:14,985
Seriously, so dramatic.

331
00:18:15,065 --> 00:18:16,705
Now I'm getting you back.

332
00:18:19,385 --> 00:18:20,345
I mean every word.

333
00:18:20,425 --> 00:18:22,065
Jaguar FireStorm.

334
00:18:34,665 --> 00:18:35,665
Idiot.

335
00:18:56,425 --> 00:19:00,665
MIDTERM EXAM DAY

336
00:19:05,785 --> 00:19:06,745
So,

337
00:19:06,825 --> 00:19:09,505
-How did the exam go?
-I'm definitely getting an A.

338
00:19:10,105 --> 00:19:11,345
Because I had a great tutor.

339
00:19:11,425 --> 00:19:12,585
And he's cute too.

340
00:19:15,465 --> 00:19:17,025
Cut out the cheesy lines.

341
00:19:18,225 --> 00:19:21,065
I'm definitely getting a high score.
Oh, right.

342
00:19:21,145 --> 00:19:23,545
Don't forget the reward.
We promised we'd go on a trip.

343
00:19:25,025 --> 00:19:28,145
Exams are finally over! Time to celebrate!

344
00:19:28,225 --> 00:19:29,905
-Let's grab something to eat.
-What should we eat?

345
00:19:29,985 --> 00:19:31,825
-Let's go eat. I'm starving.
-Let's go.

346
00:19:31,905 --> 00:19:33,425
-Where should we go?
-I'm starving already. Huh?

347
00:19:33,505 --> 00:19:34,945
Anywhere's fine. Let's go.

348
00:19:36,505 --> 00:19:37,585
Hurry up.

349
00:19:37,665 --> 00:19:39,225
I'm starving. That exam was brutal.

350
00:19:39,305 --> 00:19:43,345
-Your salmon dish is ready.
-I ordered that.

351
00:19:43,425 --> 00:19:44,945
-I ordered one too.
-I'm having some too.

352
00:19:45,025 --> 00:19:47,065
-Dig in.
-Finish it all.

353
00:19:48,705 --> 00:19:49,945
-What?
-Top it up for me.

354
00:19:50,905 --> 00:19:52,385
Thanks.

355
00:19:52,465 --> 00:19:55,505
Don't let Min see you doing that,
or she'll totally ship you two.

356
00:19:55,585 --> 00:19:56,625
Who mentioned me?

357
00:19:56,705 --> 00:19:58,665
-Nothing.
-Nothing. Never mind.

358
00:19:58,745 --> 00:20:00,345
So cute.

359
00:20:00,425 --> 00:20:03,145
-Want another bite?
-I even told Goddess Lakshmi.

360
00:20:03,225 --> 00:20:04,105
About who?

361
00:20:04,185 --> 00:20:05,825
About you, of course.

362
00:20:05,905 --> 00:20:07,825
There's only one person.

363
00:20:08,785 --> 00:20:09,745
I'm going to the restroom.

364
00:20:09,825 --> 00:20:11,025
Go ahead.

365
00:20:15,265 --> 00:20:18,465
-Let me have some.
-Me too.

366
00:20:18,545 --> 00:20:20,185
Dear customers,

367
00:20:20,265 --> 00:20:22,305
today we have salmon on special.

368
00:20:22,385 --> 00:20:23,345
Raise your hand if you'd like one.

369
00:20:23,425 --> 00:20:26,665
-Me! Me!
-Me! Me!

370
00:20:26,745 --> 00:20:29,545
-Me first!
-Indy, don't you like sashimi?

371
00:20:30,705 --> 00:20:31,745
-I do.
-Then order it.

372
00:20:31,825 --> 00:20:33,185
But I don't eat salmon.

373
00:20:33,265 --> 00:20:35,025
Oh, right. I forgot.

374
00:20:36,585 --> 00:20:38,185
Should we order one for Ter?

375
00:20:38,265 --> 00:20:41,505
-In case he wants some.
-No, he doesn't eat salmon.

376
00:20:42,705 --> 00:20:43,665
Do you want one too?

377
00:20:43,745 --> 00:20:46,385
-No, I'm full.
-Okay.

378
00:20:48,585 --> 00:20:51,505
-You're pretty close to Ter, huh?
-Oh, my life.

379
00:20:51,585 --> 00:20:53,185
You even know what he likes.

380
00:20:53,265 --> 00:20:55,025
I just saw you guys arguing earlier.

381
00:20:55,105 --> 00:20:57,745
Well, we're roommates, aren't we?

382
00:20:57,825 --> 00:20:59,225
So I know him pretty well.

383
00:21:00,105 --> 00:21:01,105
Really?

384
00:21:02,265 --> 00:21:03,265
Yeah.

385
00:21:10,185 --> 00:21:11,465
That's a lot. You eat so much.

386
00:21:12,505 --> 00:21:14,625
-Move over a bit.
-Come sit in here.

387
00:21:14,705 --> 00:21:15,825
Come sit here.

388
00:21:23,425 --> 00:21:24,425
Thanks.

389
00:21:53,305 --> 00:21:54,585
Hello.

390
00:21:56,745 --> 00:21:58,345
Um…

391
00:21:58,945 --> 00:22:00,025
Could you read my fortune?

392
00:22:02,385 --> 00:22:03,545
The shrine is closed today.

393
00:22:04,505 --> 00:22:06,585
I'll pay you. Double.

394
00:22:07,585 --> 00:22:08,945
Please.

395
00:22:13,345 --> 00:22:14,385
Come in.

396
00:22:29,185 --> 00:22:30,785
I can only read your fortune.

397
00:22:30,865 --> 00:22:33,225
I just want to know…

398
00:22:33,785 --> 00:22:35,505
who's going to confess to Ter…

399
00:22:36,105 --> 00:22:37,105
I can only read your fortune.

400
00:22:37,185 --> 00:22:39,265
…or who he has a crush on.

401
00:22:40,185 --> 00:22:41,505
I…

402
00:22:41,585 --> 00:22:43,825
can only read your fortune.

403
00:22:45,785 --> 00:22:47,065
What about Lee?

404
00:22:51,705 --> 00:22:52,905
If I say one more word,
I'll have to charge extra.

405
00:22:54,225 --> 00:22:55,985
I CAN ONLY READ YOUR FORTUNE.

406
00:23:03,025 --> 00:23:05,105
How about I read your overall
fortune instead?

407
00:23:22,545 --> 00:23:24,905
Lately, you've been lonely.
And feeling hurt.

408
00:23:24,985 --> 00:23:26,105
And paranoid.

409
00:23:26,785 --> 00:23:28,625
Damn, that's spot on.

410
00:23:28,705 --> 00:23:30,385
And The Moon card also says…

411
00:23:30,465 --> 00:23:33,025
you're overthinking,
so be careful with that.

412
00:23:42,065 --> 00:23:43,065
As for this one, I'd better not tell you.

413
00:23:43,145 --> 00:23:44,225
What?

414
00:23:44,305 --> 00:23:45,545
You can do that?

415
00:23:46,265 --> 00:23:47,945
A special service just for you.

416
00:23:49,305 --> 00:23:51,145
I want to know, fortune teller.

417
00:23:52,585 --> 00:23:54,185
When the time comes,
the universe will tell you.

418
00:23:56,225 --> 00:23:57,665
You don't say.

419
00:23:58,305 --> 00:23:59,945
Let's go somewhere to unwind.

420
00:24:00,025 --> 00:24:02,345
I know a place.
I'll send you the location.

421
00:24:07,185 --> 00:24:09,305
Fine. Don't tell me, then.

422
00:24:10,785 --> 00:24:12,025
I'll just go check it out myself.

423
00:24:33,265 --> 00:24:34,825
Morning.

424
00:24:34,905 --> 00:24:36,145
Min, Yihwa.

425
00:24:36,225 --> 00:24:37,905
Morning, Lee.

426
00:24:42,945 --> 00:24:44,505
What's going on with those two?

427
00:25:04,105 --> 00:25:06,545
Why is the vibe so tense today?

428
00:25:08,105 --> 00:25:10,425
Min and Yihwa are on their period.

429
00:25:11,665 --> 00:25:12,505
At the same time?

430
00:25:12,585 --> 00:25:14,025
Yeah.

431
00:25:27,705 --> 00:25:28,705
Are you on your period too?

432
00:25:29,745 --> 00:25:30,745
You seem pretty tense.

433
00:25:34,385 --> 00:25:35,865
Me? Tense?

434
00:25:37,265 --> 00:25:38,785
I wasn't that tense at first.

435
00:25:39,705 --> 00:25:40,985
But now I definitely am.

436
00:25:43,745 --> 00:25:45,545
If something's bothering you, just say it.

437
00:25:48,545 --> 00:25:50,905
Is there anything you're not telling me?

438
00:25:54,825 --> 00:25:55,825
Well…

439
00:25:58,705 --> 00:25:59,545
No.

440
00:26:03,265 --> 00:26:05,065
Then let me ask you this.

441
00:26:05,945 --> 00:26:08,905
You and Putter…
You're really not together, right?

442
00:26:18,185 --> 00:26:19,545
Are you suspicious of me?

443
00:26:20,465 --> 00:26:22,345
It's just that you seem…

444
00:26:22,425 --> 00:26:23,985
to care about him a lot.

445
00:26:27,305 --> 00:26:28,665
Of course I'm close to him.

446
00:26:28,745 --> 00:26:31,705
He's the one who reports
everything to my mom.

447
00:26:32,265 --> 00:26:34,185
So I have to stay on his good side.

448
00:26:35,785 --> 00:26:36,785
I get it.

449
00:26:38,305 --> 00:26:41,025
You think I'm closer to him
than I am to you, don't you?

450
00:26:45,665 --> 00:26:47,905
Hey, don't! Fuck, don't!

451
00:26:47,985 --> 00:26:48,865
Stop it!

452
00:26:48,945 --> 00:26:50,305
Ugh!

453
00:26:50,385 --> 00:26:52,225
I seriously can't take

454
00:26:52,305 --> 00:26:53,825
your straight-guy horseplay anymore.

455
00:26:53,905 --> 00:26:55,385
I take it back.

456
00:26:56,385 --> 00:26:57,385
I'm sorry.

457
00:26:59,225 --> 00:27:00,665
That's so gross.

458
00:27:03,505 --> 00:27:05,585
<i>What time today?</i>

459
00:27:09,985 --> 00:27:12,665
<i>3:40 pm. Meet me at the school gate.</i>

460
00:27:20,505 --> 00:27:21,905
Hey, Lee.

461
00:27:21,985 --> 00:27:24,025
You're walking like you're running
from the disciplinary office.

462
00:27:24,105 --> 00:27:26,625
I have to hurry. Someone might see us.

463
00:27:28,585 --> 00:27:29,905
And our date will be ruined.

464
00:27:30,505 --> 00:27:32,105
Oh, come on.

465
00:27:32,185 --> 00:27:33,945
There are plenty of other days.
We can go another time.

466
00:27:34,025 --> 00:27:35,465
But I promised.

467
00:27:50,545 --> 00:27:52,785
Hey, where are you two rushing off to?

468
00:27:52,865 --> 00:27:53,905
Where are you guys going?

469
00:27:54,625 --> 00:27:57,065
-We're going to study.
-You? Studying?

470
00:27:57,145 --> 00:27:58,305
LeeIth? Studying?

471
00:27:59,545 --> 00:28:01,065
You're actually getting serious.

472
00:28:01,145 --> 00:28:02,945
-I'm proud of you.
-Yeah, yeah.

473
00:28:03,025 --> 00:28:04,705
We're in a hurry.
We've gotta go or we'll be late.

474
00:28:04,785 --> 00:28:07,345
-Okay, see you on club day.
-See you on club day.

475
00:28:07,425 --> 00:28:08,425
Club day?

476
00:28:09,305 --> 00:28:11,145
Shit… Lee, Ter, wait!

477
00:28:12,025 --> 00:28:13,305
Shit, I just remembered something!

478
00:28:13,385 --> 00:28:15,625
Come back here, both of you!

479
00:28:15,705 --> 00:28:18,265
Mayday! Mayday!
Emergency meeting right now!

480
00:28:18,345 --> 00:28:20,705
Anyone who's already gone home,
get back to school now!

481
00:28:20,785 --> 00:28:21,905
I just remembered something!

482
00:28:21,985 --> 00:28:24,385
-Can it wait until another day?
-No, it has to be today!

483
00:28:25,105 --> 00:28:25,945
Shit…

484
00:28:26,025 --> 00:28:27,425
If we don't do it today,

485
00:28:27,505 --> 00:28:28,905
our club will be shut down!

486
00:28:28,985 --> 00:28:30,305
Move it!

487
00:28:30,985 --> 00:28:32,065
Hurry!

488
00:28:34,345 --> 00:28:36,305
-I'm hurrying already!
-Come on, hurry!

489
00:28:36,385 --> 00:28:37,785
Hey, careful! Don't spill it!

490
00:28:38,705 --> 00:28:41,065
We're supposed to submit the video today,

491
00:28:41,145 --> 00:28:42,345
or our club will lose points.

492
00:28:42,425 --> 00:28:43,305
-What?
-What?

493
00:28:43,385 --> 00:28:44,945
Why are you only telling us today?

494
00:28:45,025 --> 00:28:46,345
Actually…

495
00:28:46,425 --> 00:28:48,665
the teacher told us ages ago.
But I forgot.

496
00:28:48,745 --> 00:28:50,785
Didn't you write it down
or set a reminder?

497
00:28:50,865 --> 00:28:52,625
I stored it in my brain,
but then I forgot.

498
00:28:52,705 --> 00:28:53,825
Dumbass.

499
00:28:53,905 --> 00:28:55,225
Come on.

500
00:28:55,305 --> 00:28:56,225
Forget it for now.

501
00:28:56,305 --> 00:28:57,745
Let's figure it out first.

502
00:28:57,825 --> 00:28:58,745
No need.

503
00:28:58,825 --> 00:29:00,665
I've already thought of
my punishment for forgetting.

504
00:29:01,345 --> 00:29:03,385
Then why didn't you say so from the start?

505
00:29:03,465 --> 00:29:04,985
If I didn't hook you first,
would you listen?

506
00:29:05,065 --> 00:29:06,025
Stop dragging it out.

507
00:29:06,105 --> 00:29:07,705
-Let's go.
-Hey, wait!

508
00:29:09,465 --> 00:29:10,705
Hold on.

509
00:29:11,785 --> 00:29:12,785
Hello, where are you?

510
00:29:12,865 --> 00:29:14,585
<i>Hello, Bro. I'm here. Over this way!</i>

511
00:29:14,665 --> 00:29:17,945
-I'm here, Bro!
-Hurry up!

512
00:29:18,025 --> 00:29:19,105
What's up, Bro?

513
00:29:19,185 --> 00:29:22,025
Okay, we're filming a video exposing
the male students

514
00:29:22,105 --> 00:29:23,385
living at an all-girls school

515
00:29:23,465 --> 00:29:26,345
to promote our school
so more male students will apply.

516
00:29:26,425 --> 00:29:29,265
And then, the school can improve
the benefits for male students.

517
00:29:30,825 --> 00:29:32,465
I have to hand it to you
when it comes to content.

518
00:29:33,145 --> 00:29:34,305
Seriously, Bro. Seriously.

519
00:29:34,385 --> 00:29:36,065
That's awesome.

520
00:29:36,145 --> 00:29:37,425
So what's the plan?

521
00:29:37,505 --> 00:29:38,705
These days, it has to feel real.

522
00:29:38,785 --> 00:29:40,785
I want each of you to send me footage

523
00:29:40,865 --> 00:29:42,345
related to the school.

524
00:29:42,425 --> 00:29:44,625
I'll edit it, do the voice-over,
and that's it.

525
00:29:45,945 --> 00:29:46,865
Okay.

526
00:29:46,945 --> 00:29:48,985
-Go, go, go!
-Got it!

527
00:29:49,065 --> 00:29:51,185
Get in there! You too! Hurry up!

528
00:29:51,265 --> 00:29:52,105
Shoot plenty of it.

529
00:29:52,185 --> 00:29:53,825
Just in case we don't have enough content.

530
00:29:53,905 --> 00:29:55,265
Hurry up!

531
00:29:56,705 --> 00:29:58,385
Okay, everyone. I've turned on AirDrop.

532
00:29:58,465 --> 00:29:59,825
Send everything to my laptop.

533
00:30:04,945 --> 00:30:06,665
-I've already sent it.
-You already sent it?

534
00:30:08,265 --> 00:30:09,705
Yeah, I sent it.

535
00:30:15,305 --> 00:30:16,305
What?

536
00:30:17,905 --> 00:30:19,145
Whose footage is this?

537
00:30:23,145 --> 00:30:25,665
Judging by the order, isn't it LeeIth's?

538
00:30:28,865 --> 00:30:31,185
LeeIth has footage of Putter,

539
00:30:31,265 --> 00:30:33,865
and Putter has footage of LeeIth.

540
00:30:38,185 --> 00:30:39,465
What the hell are you guys staring at?

541
00:30:39,545 --> 00:30:43,105
Well, it's because we're roommates.

542
00:30:43,185 --> 00:30:44,465
Right? Aren't we?

543
00:30:45,065 --> 00:30:46,345
-Right? Yeah.
-Yeah, that's right.

544
00:30:47,225 --> 00:30:49,065
I think something's fishy.

545
00:30:50,865 --> 00:30:52,385
What the hell is so fishy about it?

546
00:30:52,465 --> 00:30:53,705
Prove it.

547
00:31:07,905 --> 00:31:08,865
Whoa!

548
00:31:14,145 --> 00:31:15,065
What?

549
00:31:15,145 --> 00:31:17,465
I kissed him to prove
we're strictly platonic.

550
00:31:21,185 --> 00:31:22,105
Don't!

551
00:31:23,545 --> 00:31:25,745
Hey, hey! That's enough!

552
00:31:26,665 --> 00:31:28,185
Get back to work, assholes.

553
00:31:29,345 --> 00:31:31,505
Come on, let's get this done.

554
00:31:33,265 --> 00:31:35,865
Hurry up, edit it, dub it,
so we can wrap it up.

555
00:31:55,665 --> 00:31:57,345
That's enough.

556
00:31:57,425 --> 00:32:01,665
I'm sorry for not keeping my promise.

557
00:32:01,745 --> 00:32:02,745
Mm.

558
00:32:03,265 --> 00:32:04,705
We can go another time.

559
00:32:04,785 --> 00:32:05,785
I'm not in a hurry.

560
00:32:08,385 --> 00:32:10,705
But I wanted to take you there today.

561
00:32:11,505 --> 00:32:12,705
I know.

562
00:32:12,785 --> 00:32:14,025
Let's save it for next time.

563
00:32:19,105 --> 00:32:21,065
If you could travel anywhere,
where would it be?

564
00:32:22,625 --> 00:32:23,705
Probably the beach.

565
00:32:24,865 --> 00:32:25,865
Oh,

566
00:32:26,425 --> 00:32:27,865
because Chiang Mai has no sea?

567
00:32:27,945 --> 00:32:28,985
Yeah.

568
00:32:29,065 --> 00:32:30,225
There are only mountains.

569
00:32:30,305 --> 00:32:31,305
I want to play in the water.

570
00:32:32,785 --> 00:32:35,185
Hey, I'll take you there.

571
00:32:35,265 --> 00:32:36,305
Come on.

572
00:32:38,745 --> 00:32:40,665
Hey, come on. Let's go.

573
00:32:41,265 --> 00:32:44,265
Ta-da! The Bangkok Sea. What do you think?

574
00:32:44,345 --> 00:32:45,465
Nice view, huh?

575
00:32:46,945 --> 00:32:48,745
A million-dollar view.

576
00:32:48,825 --> 00:32:50,705
For zero baht.

577
00:32:52,665 --> 00:32:53,905
Your mom paid for it, though.

578
00:32:57,385 --> 00:32:58,225
Way to kill the mood.

579
00:33:21,065 --> 00:33:22,305
Hey.

580
00:34:08,784 --> 00:34:09,945
Get in the water.

581
00:34:16,585 --> 00:34:19,105
Be careful. The waves are strong here.

582
00:34:44,425 --> 00:34:46,744
After you. This really feels like it.

583
00:34:52,465 --> 00:34:54,784
I'll let you pick the movie.
Today's Wednesday.

584
00:34:55,784 --> 00:34:57,225
Every movie is free.

585
00:34:59,945 --> 00:35:01,465
What a great deal.

586
00:35:02,825 --> 00:35:03,905
Then let's watch this one.

587
00:35:06,505 --> 00:35:09,665
It's a romance. Nice choice.

588
00:35:35,545 --> 00:35:36,905
If it were you,

589
00:35:38,585 --> 00:35:41,425
how would you confess to your friend?

590
00:35:43,785 --> 00:35:46,665
Well, I'd probably draw them a picture.

591
00:35:47,905 --> 00:35:50,345
So, you already confessed that day.

592
00:35:52,025 --> 00:35:53,185
You asked me to draw that day.

593
00:35:54,825 --> 00:35:56,345
But I wasn't drawing it for you.

594
00:35:57,505 --> 00:35:58,585
Way to kill the mood.

595
00:36:01,145 --> 00:36:02,225
You're getting cheesy again.

596
00:36:03,505 --> 00:36:05,305
You're really bad at playing it cool.

597
00:36:08,185 --> 00:36:11,105
All this time,
it's only worked because of me.

598
00:36:11,825 --> 00:36:12,905
No one suspected a thing.

599
00:36:15,225 --> 00:36:16,305
Nonsense.

600
00:36:30,545 --> 00:36:31,585
Let's watch this one.

601
00:39:17,945 --> 00:39:20,185
Talk about perfect timing.

602
00:39:21,305 --> 00:39:22,705
Hello, what's up?

603
00:39:22,785 --> 00:39:24,305
You're downstairs already?

604
00:39:24,905 --> 00:39:26,465
Shit, Indy's downstairs.

605
00:39:43,105 --> 00:39:45,825
MUSIC FESTIVAL

606
00:39:46,585 --> 00:39:47,905
Why didn't you answer my calls?

607
00:39:51,665 --> 00:39:52,625
I went…

608
00:39:55,145 --> 00:39:55,985
swimming.

609
00:39:56,905 --> 00:39:58,865
With Putter?

610
00:40:06,625 --> 00:40:07,705
It's okay.

611
00:40:08,305 --> 00:40:09,585
Can I apply?

612
00:40:09,665 --> 00:40:11,865
I secretly invited Proud too.
She's interested.

613
00:40:11,945 --> 00:40:12,985
Damn, Proud?

614
00:40:14,225 --> 00:40:16,185
Then sign up. What are you waiting for?

615
00:40:16,265 --> 00:40:18,265
So, should we discuss
which song to submit?

616
00:40:20,425 --> 00:40:21,505
Well…

617
00:40:24,065 --> 00:40:26,465
Or are you busy with something?

618
00:40:27,145 --> 00:40:28,825
Do you already have plans with Putter?

619
00:40:36,145 --> 00:40:37,745
No.

620
00:40:37,825 --> 00:40:39,305
You guys go ahead.

621
00:40:39,385 --> 00:40:40,745
I'm gonna play games.

622
00:40:40,825 --> 00:40:42,305
There are snacks in the fridge.

623
00:40:42,385 --> 00:40:43,625
Want some? I'll get them for you.

624
00:40:43,705 --> 00:40:44,745
Oh.

625
00:40:44,825 --> 00:40:45,825
It's okay.

626
00:40:46,545 --> 00:40:48,705
Oh, right. I was about to text you.

627
00:40:48,785 --> 00:40:50,785
You look cuter.

628
00:40:52,465 --> 00:40:54,585
You just look brighter.

629
00:40:55,465 --> 00:40:56,705
Are you in love or something?

630
00:40:59,745 --> 00:41:02,065
Thais really do talk nonsense. Go on.

631
00:41:02,145 --> 00:41:03,185
Come on, go sign up.

632
00:41:04,785 --> 00:41:07,305
Hurry up. Go to my room and practice.

633
00:41:08,825 --> 00:41:11,105
I'll make it up to you later.

634
00:41:21,665 --> 00:41:22,865
Hello.

635
00:41:25,345 --> 00:41:27,425
Don't hold your phone
so close to the speaker.

636
00:41:29,905 --> 00:41:31,105
My ears are killing me.

637
00:41:32,785 --> 00:41:34,985
Now then, a proper introduction.

638
00:41:35,065 --> 00:41:37,305
The newest member of Lazy Meow Meow.

639
00:41:37,385 --> 00:41:38,345
First up,

640
00:41:39,265 --> 00:41:41,305
our all-rounder drummer,

641
00:41:41,385 --> 00:41:43,825
a man of few words
but powerful beats, Leo!

642
00:41:47,345 --> 00:41:49,185
Next up,

643
00:41:49,905 --> 00:41:52,465
our bassist with slippery hands
and a slippery mind,

644
00:41:52,545 --> 00:41:54,025
Min.

645
00:41:54,105 --> 00:41:56,225
Give me a better nickname.

646
00:41:56,305 --> 00:41:57,425
Damn.

647
00:41:57,505 --> 00:42:00,265
That's so cool. That was insane, Min.

648
00:42:00,345 --> 00:42:02,345
The crazy part is we just found out
you can play, Min.

649
00:42:03,145 --> 00:42:04,145
Give us a song.

650
00:42:12,945 --> 00:42:15,785
Holy shit, that was incredible.

651
00:42:15,865 --> 00:42:18,385
Whoa, that's awesome! Come on.

652
00:42:18,465 --> 00:42:19,705
Let me join in.

653
00:42:23,145 --> 00:42:25,305
-Hey, everyone.
-Hey!

654
00:42:25,385 --> 00:42:26,785
Did Putter join the band too?

655
00:42:29,225 --> 00:42:30,465
No.

656
00:42:30,545 --> 00:42:32,985
Every band needs a manager, doesn't it?

657
00:42:33,065 --> 00:42:36,505
Taking photos and ordering food
for everyone. Isn't that good?

658
00:42:36,585 --> 00:42:39,625
It is. Then I can ship LeeIth and Putter.

659
00:42:40,865 --> 00:42:43,585
Stuff that overactive imagination back
into your head.

660
00:42:52,465 --> 00:42:53,945
Why didn't you tell me?

661
00:42:56,065 --> 00:42:58,825
It was supposed to be a surprise.
Wasn't it a good one?

662
00:43:00,425 --> 00:43:03,385
Come on, everyone. Let's play a song.

663
00:43:03,465 --> 00:43:04,905
Hey, film us for me.

664
00:43:04,985 --> 00:43:06,305
-Sure.
-Yeah, set up the camera too.

665
00:43:13,625 --> 00:43:15,985
<i>Wanna play with me?</i>

666
00:43:17,345 --> 00:43:19,625
<i>Been secretly watching you for so long</i>
<i>And you still don't know</i>

667
00:43:19,705 --> 00:43:22,345
<i>How many times</i>
<i>Have I seen you from right here?</i>

668
00:43:22,425 --> 00:43:24,985
<i>Every time you see a pup</i>
<i>You go play with it</i>

669
00:43:25,065 --> 00:43:26,945
<i>Yet with me, you act so indifferent</i>

670
00:43:27,025 --> 00:43:32,385
<i>How lucky to be born a dog</i>
<i>Getting all your love and care</i>

671
00:43:32,465 --> 00:43:35,105
<i>You only adore the pup</i>
<i>Nuzzling up for you to pet</i>

672
00:43:35,185 --> 00:43:37,465
<i>No need for approval</i>
<i>You love them right away</i>

673
00:43:37,545 --> 00:43:39,465
<i>I go to bed dreaming of being your pup</i>

674
00:43:39,545 --> 00:43:42,305
<i>So you can pet me before bed</i>
<i>Every single night</i>

675
00:43:42,385 --> 00:43:44,785
<i>Waiting at all hours</i>
<i>Keeping you from feeling sad</i>

676
00:43:44,865 --> 00:43:47,825
<i>Following you like a shadow</i>
<i>So you're never lonely</i>

677
00:44:12,665 --> 00:44:14,065
Putter.

678
00:44:16,105 --> 00:44:17,385
It's gorgeous.

679
00:44:23,785 --> 00:44:25,545
-You okay?
-I'm done.

680
00:44:25,625 --> 00:44:26,545
Look.

681
00:44:29,545 --> 00:44:31,705
Damn, you shoot so well.

682
00:44:32,665 --> 00:44:34,305
I've still got a lot to learn.

683
00:44:35,025 --> 00:44:36,225
<i>What are you doing today?</i>

684
00:44:36,305 --> 00:44:37,305
<i>Let's hang out.</i>

685
00:44:58,065 --> 00:44:59,505
<i>I'm busy today.</i>

686
00:44:59,585 --> 00:45:00,425
<i>Where are you going?</i>

687
00:45:06,625 --> 00:45:08,025
<i>What are you up to, my friend?</i>

688
00:45:10,545 --> 00:45:11,905
<i>I've got something to do.</i>

689
00:45:20,785 --> 00:45:23,705
Come on. Let's go for a walk. You in?

690
00:45:24,665 --> 00:45:25,665
-Let's go.
-Let's do it.

691
00:46:45,585 --> 00:46:47,785
So, does this make up for the beach?

692
00:46:49,385 --> 00:46:50,265
It does.

693
00:46:51,465 --> 00:46:54,065
<i>Oh, beautiful sea</i>

694
00:46:54,665 --> 00:46:56,825
<i>Beneath the bright blue sky</i>

695
00:46:58,185 --> 00:47:01,065
<i>I can see sailboats</i>

696
00:47:01,625 --> 00:47:03,345
And not just sailboats.

697
00:47:03,945 --> 00:47:07,625
There are speedboats,
banana boats, and soon, jet skis too.

698
00:47:07,705 --> 00:47:09,385
We'll work our way up,

699
00:47:09,465 --> 00:47:12,305
from a swimming pool, to the riverside,

700
00:47:12,385 --> 00:47:14,705
and next time, the sea for real.

701
00:47:16,225 --> 00:47:18,025
I hope you're not all talk.

702
00:47:39,705 --> 00:47:41,105
<i>Who's going to confess to Putter?</i>

703
00:47:41,865 --> 00:47:43,905
<i>When the time comes,</i>
<i>the universe will tell you.</i>

704
00:48:25,225 --> 00:48:28,305
<i>Since when did I start</i>
<i>feeling it this much?</i>

705
00:48:42,705 --> 00:48:44,065
DELETE POST

706
00:48:52,225 --> 00:48:55,385
SINCE WHEN DID I START
FEELING IT THIS MUCH?

707
00:49:37,145 --> 00:49:39,665
<i>The meaning of The Sun card.</i>

708
00:49:43,465 --> 00:49:44,905
<i>The truth will come to light.</i>

709
00:49:44,985 --> 00:49:47,265
<i>No secret in this world can stay hidden.</i>

710
00:50:14,545 --> 00:50:17,345
<i>Girl, I have some juicy gossip.</i>

711
00:50:37,585 --> 00:50:39,985
-Hi, LeeIth.
-You can pick the next song.

712
00:50:41,025 --> 00:50:43,945
-Hey, I want to pick the song.
-Deal.

713
00:50:44,785 --> 00:50:47,185
Next time, I'll choose my favorite song.

714
00:50:47,265 --> 00:50:48,105
Sure.

715
00:50:51,665 --> 00:50:52,625
Sure.

716
00:50:52,705 --> 00:50:54,025
Whatever Indy says, I'm in.

717
00:51:01,745 --> 00:51:02,985
What's wrong with you?

718
00:51:03,065 --> 00:51:04,385
Do you guys want anything
from the cafeteria?

719
00:51:05,025 --> 00:51:07,785
-Min, Yihwa, do you want anything?
-No.

720
00:51:13,745 --> 00:51:15,425
Are you mad at me?

721
00:51:15,505 --> 00:51:17,145
If you've got something to say,
just say it.

722
00:51:18,545 --> 00:51:20,305
I always say things straight.

723
00:51:20,385 --> 00:51:22,465
And when have you
ever been straight with me?

724
00:51:23,225 --> 00:51:24,665
Then ask me.

725
00:51:24,745 --> 00:51:26,465
Then why did you lie to me

726
00:51:26,545 --> 00:51:27,905
about going sketching with Putter?

727
00:51:29,865 --> 00:51:31,145
Why did you say you were busy?

728
00:51:39,225 --> 00:51:41,225
Just calm down first.

729
00:51:42,025 --> 00:51:44,105
I don't have a problem
with your new friend.

730
00:51:44,185 --> 00:51:46,945
I just don't get what the hell
is wrong with you.

731
00:51:50,745 --> 00:51:51,905
It's not about a new friend.

732
00:51:51,985 --> 00:51:53,465
It's not about a new friend.

733
00:51:53,545 --> 00:51:55,225
It's about you.

734
00:51:55,305 --> 00:51:57,225
If you don't want to be
friends with me anymore,

735
00:51:57,305 --> 00:51:59,065
then just say it, damn it.

736
00:52:15,025 --> 00:52:16,945
I'll go talk to Indy.

737
00:52:18,105 --> 00:52:20,145
I don't want you two
to end things like this.

738
00:52:25,105 --> 00:52:26,105
No.

739
00:52:26,825 --> 00:52:30,105
I think I need to handle this myself.

740
00:52:31,305 --> 00:52:32,665
Why?

741
00:52:34,305 --> 00:52:37,945
Because I'm the one who made that rule.

742
00:52:42,185 --> 00:52:46,585
And this evening,
I'll tell everyone in the club about us.

743
00:52:50,745 --> 00:52:52,105
Then we'll go together.

744
00:52:53,745 --> 00:52:55,345
It's not just your responsibility.

745
00:53:01,545 --> 00:53:02,665
Don't worry.

746
00:53:03,505 --> 00:53:04,945
I'll see you at the club this evening.

747
00:54:10,745 --> 00:54:12,305
-Tungtae! Tungtae!
-Tungtae! Tungtae!

748
00:54:12,385 --> 00:54:14,145
-LeeIth's over here, Bro!
-LeeIth's over here!

749
00:54:14,705 --> 00:54:15,865
Damn it, LeeIth!

750
00:54:18,025 --> 00:54:20,305
-Get up!
-What the hell are you sitting here for?

751
00:54:20,385 --> 00:54:21,385
Have you seen it?

752
00:54:21,465 --> 00:54:23,585
Those delusional idiots found
Putter's private account.

753
00:54:24,265 --> 00:54:26,465
And it looks like he has a thing for Indy.

754
00:54:28,145 --> 00:54:30,065
How do you know it's Putter's?

755
00:54:30,145 --> 00:54:33,385
Min told Summer that

756
00:54:33,465 --> 00:54:35,425
Putter typed a message,

757
00:54:35,505 --> 00:54:36,905
but accidentally posted it
to the wrong account.

758
00:54:36,985 --> 00:54:38,665
Then he deleted it and reposted it
on his private account.

759
00:54:38,745 --> 00:54:41,065
But someone was following
that private account.

760
00:54:41,585 --> 00:54:42,705
It was the exact same message,

761
00:54:42,785 --> 00:54:44,145
so they figured it out.

762
00:54:44,225 --> 00:54:45,985
Then they started screenshotting it
and shipping them.

763
00:54:46,065 --> 00:54:48,025
But it might not be him, LeeIth.

764
00:54:48,105 --> 00:54:49,265
What do you think?

765
00:54:52,545 --> 00:54:54,225
<i>You're not fast enough to avoid my eyes.</i>

766
00:54:54,305 --> 00:54:57,545
<i>#IndyPutterIsTheRealDeal</i>

767
00:54:57,625 --> 00:55:00,585
<i>It’d be nice if</i>
<i>you asked the right person.</i>

768
00:55:00,665 --> 00:55:01,825
<i>What is it?</i>

769
00:55:01,905 --> 00:55:03,585
<i>It's not this one.</i>

770
00:55:05,185 --> 00:55:06,305
Sorry, Putter.

771
00:55:06,385 --> 00:55:07,905
Yeah, it's okay.

772
00:55:07,985 --> 00:55:09,105
You're not gonna roast him?

773
00:55:09,185 --> 00:55:10,025
Indy.

774
00:55:10,105 --> 00:55:11,345
Three girls.

775
00:55:12,025 --> 00:55:13,065
Is that a new perfume?

776
00:55:14,145 --> 00:55:15,665
Indy wears the same scent.

777
00:55:19,425 --> 00:55:21,065
-Hey, Putter.
-Hey, Putter.

778
00:55:21,145 --> 00:55:23,545
-Putter!
-Putter!

779
00:55:26,225 --> 00:55:27,465
You're freaking awesome.

780
00:55:27,545 --> 00:55:29,425
-Yeah, seriously.
-Awesome!

781
00:55:29,505 --> 00:55:30,665
What are you talking about?

782
00:55:30,745 --> 00:55:32,185
You still don't get it?

783
00:55:33,785 --> 00:55:35,065
I know now.

784
00:55:36,105 --> 00:55:37,385
I know your secret.

785
00:55:38,345 --> 00:55:41,025
<i>‎All we can be is friends</i>

786
00:55:41,105 --> 00:55:44,785
<i>‎The one you love is definitely not me</i>

787
00:55:44,865 --> 00:55:51,505
<i>Time to stop dreaming</i>
<i>I never mattered to you</i>

788
00:55:51,585 --> 00:55:52,825
<i>So all this time</i>

789
00:55:53,705 --> 00:55:54,985
<i>you've liked Indy?</i>

790
00:56:17,985 --> 00:56:20,065
LeeIth, just hear me out.

791
00:56:20,145 --> 00:56:22,065
I can't date someone
who has a crush on my best friend.

792
00:56:26,585 --> 00:56:27,945
Indy!

793
00:56:29,105 --> 00:56:31,545
We know about you and LeeIth.

794
00:56:31,625 --> 00:56:34,025
I could've let it slide
when you lied to me.

795
00:56:34,105 --> 00:56:35,185
Well, he likes you.

796
00:56:35,265 --> 00:56:38,185
But weren't you
the one who made that damn rule?

797
00:56:38,265 --> 00:56:39,865
And now you're the one breaking it.

798
00:56:39,945 --> 00:56:41,305
I'm quitting this club.

799
00:56:41,385 --> 00:56:43,665
I never wanted to join
this damn club anyway.

800
00:56:43,745 --> 00:56:47,905
NO DATING SOMEONE CLOSE TO YOU!

